  <layout>One page of text; margin notes left (small italic side notes beside the paragraphs); printed footnote at the foot of the text block.</layout>
  <page_number>56</page_number>
  <running_head>DE CRVCE</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="1" caput="13" para="true">CAP. XIII.</l>
    <l n="2" para="true">
      <i>Etiam liberi quidam in Crucem da-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>ta, sed viliores aut nocentiores :</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>ut Latrones, Sicarii, Falsarii,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>atque alibi &amp; Fures.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6" para="true">{a}QVid autem in liberis? Rara</l>
    <l n="7">crux, ut prædixi. Quin</l>
    <l n="8">removere prorsus ab hoc genere</l>
    <l n="9">Lactantius videatur, ubi de</l>
    <l n="10">Christo : <i>Cur si Deus fuit, &amp; mori</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>voluit, non saltem aliquo honesto</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>genere mortis affectus est? cur po-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>tissimum Cruce? cur infami ge-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>nere supplicii? quod etiam homine</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>libero, quamvis nocente, videatur</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>indignum.</i> Sed frænanda ea as-</l>
    <l n="17">sertio est : &amp; cive quidem in-</l>
    <l n="18">digna Crux, nec credo usurpa-</l>
    <l n="19">tam in eos nisi præter leges, &amp;</l>
    <l n="20">per sævitiam. viliores liberi, &amp;</l>
    <l n="21">provinciales, non ab ea profecto</l>
    <l n="22">immunes. Atque hæc crimina in</l>
    <l n="23" type="foot" para="true">1 Lib. iv. Inst. cap. xxvi.</l>
  </main_text>
  <marginalia>
    <note letter="a" side="left" at="Quin removere prorsus" line_from="7" line_to="7">
      <i>Crux indigna liberi.</i>
    </note>
    <note side="left" at="Atque hæc crimina" line_from="22" line_to="22">
      <i>Præfertim civibus.</i>
    </note>
  </marginalia>
  <notes>Marginal notes "Crux indigna liberi." and "Præfertim civibus." are small italic side notes on the left; the footnote number 1 is marked in the text after "Lactantius". Printed text in the lower left is a footnote line. Some words are slightly blurred; "Lactantius" and "Falsarii" read with reasonable confidence.</notes>
